 "intro": "Near Suthul in Numidia, winter 110-109 BC. Jugurtha, the Numidian king, has bribed Roman senators and generals for years. You are Aulus Postumius Albinus, commanding while your brother, the consul, is in Rome.",
 "debrief": "In Sallust’s account, Aulus besieged Suthul in winter, then followed Jugurtha, who pretended to negotiate while bribing his officers. A night attack on the camp succeeded when a Ligurian cohort and Thracian horse deserted and a centurion let the enemy in. The Romans fled to a hill and had to pass under the yoke and leave Numidia. The Senate rejected the treaty, and Metellus was sent to restore the war. Jugurtha is said to have called Rome ‘a city for sale’. The other choices are what-ifs.",
